.page pkill 1 signal processes by name

# SYNOPSIS
*pkill* [*-*_SIGNAL_] _NAME_

# DESCRIPTION
`pkill` sends a signal (SIGTERM unless one is given, by name or number) to every process whose name contains _NAME_. It never signals itself.

# EXIT STATUS
0 if some process was signalled, 1 if none matched, 2 for bad usage.

# EXAMPLES
    pkill sleep
    pkill -9 spell

# SEE ALSO
kill(1), pidof(1), ps(1)
